    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d635">

                <pb facs="0533" n="521" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg521"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.248/791: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé at Tangier</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Childs</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tangier</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-11-22T16:00:00+01:00">November 22,
                            1942—4 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 6:07 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>681. The Chief of the Diplomatic Cabinet of the High Commissariat at Tetuán
                    telephoned on behalf of General Orgaz to state that the three American planes
                    which made forced landings in Spanish Morocco on November 8 have been sent this
                    morning to Madrid in accordance with instructions of the Spanish Government.</p>
                <pb facs="0534" n="522" xml:id="pg522"/>
                <p>I asked how they were sent and the statement was made that no details were
                    available.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Madrid.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Childs</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
